
"I" commands: I x = edit item x
              IN w,x,y,z = input music on staff w


I x = go into EDIT mode starting with item x.  If no number follows 'I',
      usually the last item entered or edited will come up for editing.
      See the 'E' help (Edit) for details.


IN p2,p3,p4,p5 -- starts the main music input system.  P2 = the staff number 
           where the music will be put.  The other parameters are those 
           normally entered when a musical staff is to be displayed.  The 
           other parameters will be used for the creation of the staff.  
           See help for Code 8 for details.  If a staff at the given p2 
           position already exists the higher parameters will be ignored.

           For complete details on the input procedure, see the main SCORE
           manual.


INV = inverted mordant

-------------------------------------------------------------------------end---
